From 2076e95096ea8acb781e24b0c29677a0ddf21530 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:52:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(pwa): R6.1 small fix - cache-control precedence,
 case-insensitive query names, stale-worker first visit

Incremental after baseline + R4 + R5 + R6. Draft; not deployed.
- sw.js: no-store/private/no-cache can never be overridden by immutable; sensitive query
  parameter names matched case-insensitively (write prevention and cache scrub);
  version handshake so the recovery page can tell the current worker from an older one
- register-sw.js: purge legacy caches again on controllerchange
- staleWorkerGuard: before the recovery tokens are used, unregister an old controlling
  worker, delete legacy caches and reload once with the fragment intact; fail closed
  (blocked) if a stale worker survives
- tests: focused SW/guard suites; Chromium scenarios for first direct visit under an old
  worker (fixed build and previous-build negative control) and account A recovery while
  account B's session is stored

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NvuEKCqEak8vUZ3RsxZA4i
